          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most home shops, the DeWalt DW735X is the planer to buy: two feed speeds, 13-inch capacity, included tables and strong parts support. Choose the Makita 2012NB if noise matters, the WEN PL1326 or Cutech 40200H-CT if you want a helical head for figured or reclaimed wood, and the DW734 if you plane only occasionally and want to spend less.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you pick, remember what a planer does: it makes faces parallel and boards consistent in thickness. Give it a flat reference face, feed with the grain, take light passes, leave parts long to deal with snipe, and connect dust collection before the first board goes through.
